messages.content:
The **comma** indicates the **shortest pause**. It is used:

1. to separate **three or more words of the same part of speech** (nouns, verbs, adjectives, adverbs);
2. to mark off **words in apposition**;
3. to mark off the **Nominative of Address**;
4. after an **Absolute Construction**;
5. before and after a **Participial Phrase** (that could be expanded into a clause);
6. to separate **words, phrases or clauses inserted** into the body of a sentence;
7. to separate a **Subordinate (Adverb) Clause** from the rest of the sentence;
8. to mark off a **direct quotation** from the rest of the sentence;
9. to **avoid the repetition of a verb**;
10. to mark off a **Non-Defining Relative Clause**.
